 "stem": "Solve the equation ${=a}x^2 - {=B}x + {=C} = 0$ by factorising the left side. Write the solution set, giving any non-whole root as a fraction in simplest form.",
 "solution": [
  "The left side has a leading coefficient ${=a}$, so look for a factorisation $({=a}x - {=r})(x - {=s})$.",
  "Check: ${=a}x^2 - {=a*s}x - {=r}x + {=C} = {=a}x^2 - {=B}x + {=C}$, which is correct.",
  "So $({=a}x - {=r})(x - {=s}) = 0$.",
  "Either ${=a}x - {=r} = 0$, so $x = \\frac{{=r}}{{=a}}$, or $x - {=s} = 0$, so $x = {=s}$.",
  "The solution set is $\\{\\frac{{=r}}{{=a}}, {=s}\\}$."
 ],
